 basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db067e3e-7bda-5f89-ac04-b1307dd15481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452305} {:answer/id #uuid "22258483-ea45-5772-80af-642cced16361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db067e3e-7bda-5f89-ac04-b1307dd15481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452305} :answer-field/id #uuid "87d25a98-a59c-59