and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{B}=[T]_{C}^{-1}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{C}=[T]_{B}^{-1}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dbfc974-64a1-5ba8-a98a-3c44ced3256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452317} {:answer/id #uuid "4692bc9a-0874-5399-a418-98fb85a5cec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dbfc974-64a1-5ba8-a98a-3c44ced3256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452317} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e47d84-f057-5e0a-ae70-ec0d33904e89" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420fa2b5-f5a7-5d27-bc3d-9bbf0b0cd31b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452319} {:answer/id #uuid "27f8b042-1a66-5c50-9a92-c6c664837fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f8b042-1a66-5c50-9a92-c6c664837fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452320} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e76e66-d34f-5c65-9093-a22e5839e130" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d6839f-b647-50f5-9788-3ee7b2fa1f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452321} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4185c8-8f28-5d02-aeb6-193573874b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d6839f-b647-50f5-9788-3ee7b2fa1f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452321} :answer-field/id #uuid "883ab182-da38-5ef9-bdd1-6c14d39cea71" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2667e6b9-8784-550d-a849-0ee298d78d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-97078" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Im}(T)={0}$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The condition $\\text{rank}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b9e07b5-9f0c-5f9e-b5e0-dd0bb5ddbb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452329} {:answer/id #uuid "d14bb30d-305a-547d-9203-a605f0933196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b9e07b5-9f0c-5f9e-b5e0-dd0bb5ddbb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident