db/ref 17592186452465} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0d6501-f9de-5629-932b-a57f8dc171b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "288f57ed-f71f-52e4-aa4d-9812c1e3a401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452465} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce30fe09-518e-5ee9-b44b-912d5a059e61" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1c970e5-75bc-5ce7-946f-a4ae8b32b111" :question/math-academy-id "q-97960" :question/problem "If $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\lambda =1$ is an eigenvalue of $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C-I$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(C-I)\\ne 2$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(C-I)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{2} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=2=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=C-I.$\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that if $\\lambda =1$ is an eigenvalue of $C,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(C-I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $C.$ As a result, the matrix $M=C-I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $M=C-I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(C-I)\\ne 2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $M=C-I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(C-I)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "775c219f-a459-55cb-a155-865e3fee7ae2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452467} {:answer/id #uuid "3ffb7501-a137-566a-82b1-7897016fb94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ffb7501-a137-566a-82b1-7897016fb94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452468} :answer-field/id #uuid "365204e9-984b-5368-9d39-59ebec92b9e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25fe10ad-b6fd-51a0-ae35-69c2a8fbad6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452469} {:answer/id #uuid "082ed9ac-ae1b-5302-8e14-5b74ae93b90b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25fe10ad-b6fd-51a0-ae35-69c2a8fbad6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452469} :answer-field/id #uuid "470374fb-21bf-5e7b-9721-41f5a726ab31" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b81eebb0-7957-5576-828c-99384c50a06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452471} {:answer/id #uuid "b516c0cf-2ba1-5ba9-8852-4382e9ac3ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b81eebb0-7957-5576-828c-99384c50a06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452471} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8bd4bfb-634d-5ae5-aa62-0dafe1569a4e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7aa7ebc3-80d5-541f-813e-64c8db0cc171" :question/math-academy-id "q-97962" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}(A-3I)={R}^{3}$\n- **II.** $A-3I$ is singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =3$ is an eigenvalue of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $3\\times 3$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=3=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $3$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A-3I) & =3-\\text{nullity}(A-3I) \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{Col}(A-3I)={R}^{3}.$\n\n- Statements II is false. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0,$ we obtain that $A-3I$ must be non-singular.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $M=A-3I$ is non-singular, then $(A-3I)x=0$ has only zero solution. As a result, $\\lambda =3$ can not be an eigenvalue of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2cedf5f-ea78-598b-8fea-86eb4930a16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452473} {:answer/id #uuid "ac501363-d562-542c-8971-fa619b64fb93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac501363-d562-542c-8971-fa619b64fb93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452474} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed2e22e-171c-554d-a637-c726d3aaa309" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "941dacde-a17c-5765-910f-5bc4839a1386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452475} {:answer/id #uuid "5f487188-0cec-5f38-9e34-e190f507bb5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f487188-0cec-5f38-9e34-e190f507bb5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452476} :answer-field/id #uuid "611e09b5-b47a-5519-9300-6bc0ece8a2f0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0044e830-172d-574e-b097-e1ebe25e1adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452477} {:answer/id #uuid "4200c14b-bbe6-5725-adaa-903da877df9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0044e830-172d-574e-b097-e1ebe25e1adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452477} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef6a8d9-228c-5e0b-8e7a-462c8a409290" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "651bcec7-c2ce-52d1-b1e2-d8f7e6384008" :question/math-academy-id "q-97969" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A-3I)=4,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0$\n- **II.** $A-3I$ is invertible\n- **III.** $\\lambda =3$ is an eigenvalue of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $4$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(A-3I) & =4-\\text{rank}(A-3I) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0,$ we obtain that $A-3I$ must be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $M=A-3I$ is invertible, then $(A-3I)x=0$ has only zero solution. As a result, $\\lambda =3$ can not be an eigenvalue of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d33d9c39-fb68-5072-8e1d-d5100f882d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452479} {:answer/id #uuid "31f89fd5-7b10-551c-bc20-cccf8c2d412f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d33d9c39-fb68-5072-8e1d-d5100f882d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452479} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a700a6-056d-5fbf-9c15-802b0bdd40bd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f33abab6-7da2-5b60-9d2f-3f60b47ce8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452481} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9de0a6-d221-54ed-ad32-0d48a983af48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d9de0a6-d221-54ed-ad32-0d48a983af48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452482} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec61757-aa1d-5552-94ae-87ef06754a16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9364d49b-0c70-5f53-9afc-58a6465fdfe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452483} {:answer/id #uuid "bb43d0d6-435a-59ca-b0d6-dd54c6d2f55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9364d49b-0c70-5f53-9afc-58a6465fdfe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452483} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d70d8de-2041-5147-b2df-9b23496268ca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fb578155-2783-5751-8e62-1deb89778f31" :question/math-academy-id "q-97970" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(B-I)=1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}(B-I)={R}^{3}$\n- **II.** $B-I$ is singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =1$ is not an eigenvalue of $B$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $3\\times 3$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=3=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $3$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(B-I) & =3-\\text{nullity}(B-I) \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(B-I)\\ne 3,$ according to invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{Col}(B-I)\\ne {R}^{3}.$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(B-I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $B-I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $M=B-I$ is singular, then $(B-I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =1$ is an eigenvalue of $B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2408efc0-effa-5d1a-95bf-4e5888eb4e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452485} {:answer/id #uuid "478fc76b-1ffb-5eba-9444-fb9a5daab721" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2408efc0-effa-5d1a-95bf-4e5888eb4e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452485} :answer-field/id #uuid "298cd9f6-0f4b-5d91-b1e2-380da3c049cf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453090} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890097e8-1b87-5c8b-80f8-73adc10117b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452487} {:answer/id #uuid "194e8931-2c02-5f42-b19b-625e045d7857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "890097e8-1b87-5c8b-80f8-73adc10117b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452487} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a5a7b14-0732-5180-838e-5db043472ec8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453091} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88db7284-406b-5896-82c0-024eb4192579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452489} {:answer/id #uuid "35417b18-69fa-55aa-bd77-4e154b50f8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35417b18-69fa-55aa-bd77-4e154b50f8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452490} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d73097d-9167-5ae9-ac40-5d49927706d1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "89915cc7-c25f-5711-a62f-10d7e3f1b8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97972" :question/problem "If $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(C-2I)=1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}(C-2I)={R}^{2}$\n- **II.** $C-2I$ is non-singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{2} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=2=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $2$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=2.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(C-2I) & =2-\\text{nullity}(C-2I) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{Col}(C-2I)\\ne {R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statements II is false. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(C-2I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $C-2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that if $M=C-2I$ is singular, then $(C-2I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $C.$ As a result, $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4ccb0fb-57b3-54cc-9a0e-7b3b2ec086c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452491} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0736bf-0992-5540-92e4-4db3dc860d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4ccb0fb-57b3-54cc-9a0e-7b3b2ec086c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452491} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7a2ad23-7a6f-5d92-beff-9522a7a1c6e4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4c9d99e-8bcf-530d-a35b-845c74343724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452493} {:answer/id #uuid "b94d0759-6f74-5338-954d-fc2d4ed8aa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b94d0759-6f74-5338-954d-fc2d4ed8aa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452494} :answer-field/id #uuid "eabb1107-ac4d-5f76-9ad8-0708cf4bdbd2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee5ed75-acac-56ef-98ed-57d5822de8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452495} {:answer/id #uuid "537989db-6a16-5fcc-aa37-3d4aa93c947c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "537989db-6a16-5fcc-aa37-3d4aa93c947c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452496} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f83e84-79e0-5f94-a3f0-7b675d59f092" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "68bc418d-6421-5050-b933-2a80a591867e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97975" :question/problem "If $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(C+3I)=2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Null}(C+3I)={0}$\n- **II.** $C+3I$ is singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =-3$ is an eigenvalue of $C$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $4$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(C+3I) & =4-\\text{rank}(C+3I) \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{Null}(C+3I)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(C+3I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $C-3I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that if $M=C+3I$ is singular, then $(C+3I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $C.$ As a result, $\\lambda =-3$ is an eigenvalue of $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152225 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "04926916-8e08-5401-a57b-3fd333741913" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors Using Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1edb45bd-5686-5bd3-a5e8-39434b7936e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451305} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdaca35-4a5c-5775-b375-7f5a62df0513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fdaca35-4a5c-5775-b375-7f5a62df0513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451306} :answer-field/id #uuid "fda9bab3-48aa-590a-8fbb-e6278bd3979b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f942fb-0b51-5721-a798-3ef7b79f314c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451307} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b2bb2e-ef53-5665-874e-acf997870797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f942fb-0b51-5721-a798-3ef7b79f314c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451307} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3ae7022-ac6d-50ac-949c-c361f871d0d9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a867c05-749f-52ca-8d48-1539d08a5b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451309} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0f0e57-f4cb-5e3a-b938-abd9cd17f104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb0f0e57-f4cb-5e3a-b938-abd9cd17f104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451310} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ed7379-1768-5e75-a724-8e30b56031fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c08bbf4-33fd-53d2-9498-4e914b813e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109239" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }z\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A+I$ and $A-2I$ on the nonzero vectors $u,v,w,x,$ $y$ and $z$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A$\n- **II.** $u$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A$\n- **III.** $x$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\nv\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A+1I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps, \nthe vector $v$ is a generalzed eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding  to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since \n\n$$\nu\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }v,\n$$\n\n and $v\\ne 0,$ \nthe vector $u$ is **not**  an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding  to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\nx\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }z\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\ni.e. $A-2I$ maps $x$ to $0$ in $3$ steps, \nthe vector $x$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ \ncorresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd89ee68-349c-5c55-bfb4-0640100d85d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451317} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0d0530-fb2a-55ee-8c99-4b946a8d080d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f0d0530-fb2a-55ee-8c99-4b946a8d080d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451318} :answer-field/id #uuid "32ce223a-7bf9-5b24-9d75-5a1ee1be8cee" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452506} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80aff2bb-c529-532f-bd61-5a4a757274f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451319} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8b817d-950d-56d2-a00f-a66cc027dd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80aff2bb-c529-532f-bd61-5a4a757274f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451319} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea9e0400-ff35-582c-afa0-5b642cb65d38" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b20a8fdb-8267-5e02-9526-345d5877f1ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451321} {:answer/id #uuid "8b8bdf3d-57db-5827-9f8f-4a457f333e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b8bdf3d-57db-5827-9f8f-4a457f333e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451322} :answer-field/id #uuid "46443e21-8812-5903-b11e-26709577b9c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ea55d3c-3433-59ef-97d4-45fcd98ab0e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-140896" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $5\\times 4$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The columns of $Q$ are orthogonal\n\n- **II.** $Q$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix\n\n- **III.** $R$ is a  square  matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthogonal.\n\n- Statement II is false. $Q$ should be a $5\\times 4$  matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $R$ must be a $4\\times 4$ upper triangular matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef9dba6-3f12-5da9-b1c0-57877064fcd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451323} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccbf279-9ed0-556d-9395-eaabb82722b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ef9dba6-3f12-5da9-b1c0-57877064fcd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451323} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e589c4-8feb-50f2-94e5-91dc5bf78939" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452509} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47423d03-c26d-53a6-97f0-da0ec40e24ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451325} {:answer/id #uuid "59929f29-b3e2-5f68-ad2f-45acb0eee989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59929f29-b3e2-5f68-ad2f-45acb0eee989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451326} :answer-field/id #uuid "947adca6-648c-56d1-8cd2-dda98433a243" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d589cba1-1f3b-5854-9859-9dd1c62ec2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451327} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c8f22c-d237-5016-ab0c-213ce6e6e57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d589cba1-1f3b-5854-9859-9dd1c62ec2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451327} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee67563d-5792-5feb-9fa1-bed677e18320" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1442b18-9e38-5f57-94c8-12000a66d6da" :question/math-academy-id "q-140897" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is an $n\\times m$  matrix\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)$ is spanned by the columns of $Q$\n- **III.** $R$ is a $m\\times m$ matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. $Q$ should be an $m\\times n$ matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A),$ they span $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\n- Statement III is false. $R$ must be an $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124521 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9d77214-796e-558f-a364-00ae3e25cc13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3443de64-0676-5770-92c8-866233b3cf8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451329} {:answer/id #uuid "901fe7d0-00db-5d2b-bbbe-46afcbf47bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3443de64-0676-5770-92c8-866233b3cf8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451329} :answer-field/id #uuid "92a67864-fc33-5ecf-8c84-7b60097bcbae" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a924bc-04c3-5242-9b40-d555e76f1a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451331} {:answer/id #uuid "7007492f-f2e7-51ca-a49a-711d1d61f5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86a924bc-04c3-5242-9b40-d555e76f1a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451331} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1eb8ec-220b-56c6-9fb0-7009727726eb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c634fe05-9622-5bb0-8a7a-383e16e613d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451333} {:answer/id #uuid "298354bf-6e73-5d58-bebe-1e6824b6781d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "298354bf-6e73-5d58-bebe-1e6824b6781d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451334} :answer-field/id #uuid "51cb5c24-3e00-5e7d-af9c-2caa5063b2cd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7c2a831-facf-5fcc-90d0-c92cd81e88a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-141483" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $T:{R}^{6}\\to {R}^{6}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T,$ and ${{v}_{1}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Ker}(T)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{rank}(T)=6$\n- **II.** $T$ is a bijection\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{6}$ into ${R}^{6},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=6 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${{v}_{1}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Ker}(T),$ we must have that $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$ and by the invertible matrix theorem, $T$ is not invertible. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $T$ is not invertible, $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 6,$ the transformation $T$ is not a bijection.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${{v}_{1}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Ker}(T),$ we must have that $\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim(Ker}(T))=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9815692-a138-50b9-b4b5-53d1deb36416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451341} {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d41a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d41a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451342} :answer-field/id #uuid "66207179-6782-51a7-8c9c-26b58946b0d4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb7403c-1de8-5af0-a703-e840aa64edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451343} {:answer/id #uuid "258dfd42-9353-508c-8008-3bf0dbe86ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bb7403c-1de8-5af0-a703-e840aa64edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451343} :answer-field/id #uuid "95bc3e49-a85f-5996-a916-5f5842714a44" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba72e82-49bf-51a3-b88b-521926f583b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451345} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc155c3-cd22-58ba-9542-04ba60e1df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc155c3-cd22-58ba-9542-04ba60e1df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451346} :answer-field/id #uuid "9358e9ed-4724-59aa-b3e0-47a55115aa88" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd19f076-6276-574d-a171-58c6f862f950" :question/math-academy-id "q-157239" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =5[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5-2-3 \\\\ -10+1+9 \\\\ -5-1+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=5,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0346398f-65b8-5bd3-b0f9-8b628f52a353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452221} {:answer/id #uuid "bceb1ecc-febc-5631-a278-5aed524c28fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bceb1ecc-febc-5631-a278-5aed524c28fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452222} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cbf390-2de4-5d0c-9c7a-49c1601d1072" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452958} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3b4bd9b-5b77-560c-a577-20bdb4c3f47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452223} {:answer/id #uuid "dedc586f-9e2a-5d88-add5-529a718afa93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dedc586f-9e2a-5d88-add5-529a718afa93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452224} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78d5e63-ee82-56c8-9657-4763f39441dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c92a537c-38be-543f-9b04-f1d82d249904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452225} {:answer/id #uuid "e48f546a-1da8-5e18-b960-859e9f202044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e48f546a-1da8-5e18-b960-859e9f202044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452226} :answer-field/id #uuid "120438b3-dec2-597e-a996-fd9ef95e4b98" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14a18e20-8a94-54a8-afff-0a503b7d967c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95916" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The columns of $Q$ are orthonormal\n\n- **II.** $Q$ is a square matrix\n\n- **III.** $R$ is a square matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthonormal.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $Q$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa96bbef-e60b-5938-afd9-9aecce3662a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452227} {:answer/id #uuid "fc82ac14-9f60-5ff5-abf6-9be439d5811c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa96bbef-e60b-5938-afd9-9aecce3662a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452227} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe0a7f0-668f-540b-a54e-2bb0427d1d40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0037e982-4e96-568d-9977-84d06128905e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452229} {:answer/id #uuid "72d0b427-e976-5eed-8e23-5bc0a65dd9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72d0b427-e976-5eed-8e23-5bc0a65dd9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452230} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6a5e16-c6e0-5de3-b5c7-56166731c92b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452962} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ffe0134-9e43-5357-bfb9-2d702d98cc8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452231} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c660a-4b11-554a-9592-b3bbc7fe081e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa4c660a-4b11-554a-9592-b3bbc7fe081e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452232} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9d8be5-9c71-5d23-9c41-8e0eb84f478a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2d40cdd9-dee2-5236-bb35-1c36eb46fb25" :question/math-academy-id "q-95922" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $4\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $R$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n- **III.** The columns of $Q$ are orthonormal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. $Q$ should be a $4\\times 2$ matrix, so it is not square.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, $Q$ must be an orthogonal matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ca319c5-9f62-51e3-b670-611fc8a8daaa" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Critical Point Using the Second Partial Derivatives Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cbcaa0-0a4b-5073-ad88-c02a4ba1a019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451299} {:answer/id #uuid "375e98ca-c238-53ff-beba-897b64cc63a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62cbcaa0-0a4b-5073-ad88-c02a4ba1a019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451299} :answer-field/id #uuid "652213cb-11aa-5dea-a4bc-3b9c8b1c355c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b0d48c5-2f2c-5055-908e-0dc95f5f7282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451301} {:answer/id #uuid "61b6f0c7-25e4-5be3-b321-0d0f90827d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b6f0c7-25e4-5be3-b321-0d0f90827d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451302} :answer-field/id #uuid "d71cb01d-fa4d-51c3-8af9-10186ba20c84" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd7d602-b04e-508c-8f43-638a3bb96a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451303} {:answer/id #uuid "cafd6976-b47f-5881-a12d-13755ea64993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cafd6976-b47f-5881-a12d-13755ea64993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451304} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a57395c-fb2f-5e27-af13-56da5d453d17" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2adfa73-7e18-5d5d-8163-694e5efa8a14" :question/math-academy-id "q-104980" :question/problem "The function $f(x,y)$ has Hessian matrix\n\n$$\n{∇}^{2}f(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2(y-3) & 2(x+1) \\\\ 2(x+1) & (y-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(-1,3).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $H(-1,3)<0$\n- **II.** $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(-1,3)>0$\n- **III.** The second partial derivative test is inconclusive" :question/worked-solution "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ then:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$;\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a.$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a.$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivative test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the Hessian at $(-1,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∇}^{2}f(-1,3)=[\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}+2(3-3) & 2(-1+1) \\\\ 2(-1+1) & (3-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The Hessian determinant is\n\n$$\nH(-1,3)=det({∇}^{2}f(-1,3))=1(0)-0(0)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true because\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(-1,3)=1>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true because $H(-1,3)=0,$ so the second partial derivative test is inconclusive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162013 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c67d532-acd9-5231-a27f-d39084863e01" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Spectral Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb7dde31-bde1-58e8-ad71-ec6b2e8b2319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451311} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca9aaad-54c8-5fad-9a03-14113c01dc8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7dde31-bde1-58e8-ad71-ec6b2e8b2319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451311} :answer-field/id #uuid "e741fb79-46a4-593a-9d56-3df9c7384c94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05cc96c4-9bd0-5ec2-9c67-70c12fe56748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451313} {:answer/id #uuid "71be77cb-f2a0-5da9-a71b-0d54bf22920e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05cc96c4-9bd0-5ec2-9c67-70c12fe56748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451313} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fda6962-d111-5d52-9d97-94bb5cf1b992" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "757e1e41-d4bd-5b02-ae6c-09acb0b026a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451315} {:answer/id #uuid "ae88a715-f3a8-55f4-890a-5a6165ebc0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae88a715-f3a8-55f4-890a-5a6165ebc0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451316} :answer-field/id #uuid "c19a4f3d-993f-546f-aa3d-c187f50b1a7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb8cc465-a001-5ad5-bfcd-11eb17855f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-140844" :question/problem "Given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is not diagonalizable\n- **II.** $A$ must have $4$ integer eigenvalues\n- **III.** If  $\\alpha $ is an eigenvalue of $A$ with the multiplicity $2,$ then the dimension of the eigenspace for the eigenvalue $\\alpha $ is $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the spectral theorem, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable, so, $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real but not necessarily integers.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the theorem, the dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b08f7a-3777-5f1a-a9eb-461a2fd0414f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451335} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1dc0f1-cd98-5509-9477-51d011494a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8b08f7a-3777-5f1a-a9eb-461a2fd0414f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451335} :answer-field/id #uuid "57869de9-6ee9-5e0b-90f9-6810fc1f801e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c06a9fc-e9e1-5f78-abd6-96a1dabad6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451337} {:answer/id #uuid "e431efe4-4133-5a40-bbcf-62064ac9644b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e431efe4-4133-5a40-bbcf-62064ac9644b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451338} :answer-field/id #uuid "308a1332-e85b-5404-b4a5-ba01221b22ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9313834d-4423-5042-bc49-9390326be415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451339} {:answer/id #uuid "28ce3ebb-bcf9-5d61-a603-60625891c0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28ce3ebb-bcf9-5d61-a603-60625891c0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451340} :answer-field/id #uuid "237be3da-ec76-5d1e-936e-544f31cdde31" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b742394a-cffb-5df9-9fbd-181d0debffeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-143683" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A$ is *any* matrix, then ${A}^{3}$ is always symmetric.\n- **II.** The sum of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- **III.** The difference of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{3}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}-{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A-B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7e5456c-c3dd-5a0d-b1c2-3704fc8684a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451347} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3a06ba-b64e-5195-8730-c9b460991557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7e5456c-c3dd-5a0d-b1c2-3704fc8684a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451347} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1d9b580-5d43-50e2-927e-f8ae49947f12" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452521} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44f80825-4dc0-5703-964c-52ef15f73d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451349} {:answer/id #uuid "183ba4dd-4b07-51c8-addc-3f2d2bef0202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183ba4dd-4b07-51c8-addc-3f2d2bef0202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451350} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e54440b-ec3a-55ca-8152-eddfc8c269f2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd8399ad-e6d4-5375-a818-f30592990e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451351} {:answer/id #uuid "171f1a31-d670-547d-9146-cec5d20385e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171f1a31-d670-547d-9146-cec5d20385e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451352} :answer-field/id #uuid "b104c177-2725-5efd-84ea-448298f66c5d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e41ff16d-c666-5918-91e3-4e187ca2af95" :question/math-academy-id "q-37387" :question/problem "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $C$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =5$ is an eigenvalue of $C$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $4$th column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-\\lambda )\\cdot (5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )^{2}\\cdot ((2-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )+20) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +14) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +14$ we have that the only real eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (with algebraic multiplicity $2$). \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfbaf102-c0df-5e93-9fdd-76ff8e170914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451507} {:answer/id #uuid "bd856043-9bf5-545a-9dab-355b675c30de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfbaf102-c0df-5e93-9fdd-76ff8e170914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451507} :answer-field/id #uuid "17379ff6-7738-574d-b3f4-b367ff0dfb86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eacdbb44-ca0c-548a-9e83-9c47d872f78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451509} {:answer/id #uuid "f26307df-edf9-5e2f-ae55-61a18a228540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eacdbb44-ca0c-548a-9e83-9c47d872f78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451509} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1aea80c-069f-5199-b8cf-083b0c70f9f9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d27925-4f17-57c7-83c0-083d924358a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451511} {:answer/id #uuid "b187a096-71e0-5c74-af3c-85207909140b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b187a096-71e0-5c74-af3c-85207909140b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451512} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f7c0e5-f396-5066-adbe-dbe1244d165d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96c9a429-d310-55eb-845b-95fc86ca78d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71448" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-2y+z=0$ and $x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86ec9910-e0fd-500c-a549-944d8205800e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451789} {:answer/id #uuid "5a37d4f9-58db-5ba8-88b3-85410ad5ea6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a37d4f9-58db-5ba8-88b3-85410ad5ea6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451790} :answer-field/id #uuid "d02090ef-d4ce-52dc-a572-f7d577aef6d1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd5e478-5cfa-5b4b-b744-a3677754f14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451791} {:answer/id #uuid "0b89ae10-1176-5228-9818-87068f6baeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b89ae10-1176-5228-9818-87068f6baeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451792} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f49c755-7208-571d-b62b-fa250286bf1d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d81aeff-94a5-5d39-a36b-e4ef94203480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451793} {:answer/id #uuid "1923b6cb-681f-5678-aa63-c64a0628a021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d81aeff-94a5-5d39-a36b-e4ef94203480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451793} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba776b6a-55ef-5233-8b4a-47f605e790d5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6753a04-a08e-5bc2-a11a-2cad03fb8d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80800" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =-14$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-\\lambda )\\cdot (-14-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-14-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +14)\\lambda (\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =2,$ $\\lambda =-2,$ $\\lambda =0,$ and $\\lambda =-14$  (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e12609b7-286b-50a8-8373-a331d60ab904" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f285c5-f28d-52d7-8edb-dc3cd9308f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451845} {:answer/id #uuid "de316b3c-8465-5f0f-9e1d-c901b94e2cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de316b3c-8465-5f0f-9e1d-c901b94e2cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451846} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bbe03ec-cd1a-5f9e-bdaa-621344b8730a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452770} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c2821d1-dbdf-57db-8669-559772eabf32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451847} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b316c-fd27-57d7-ae6d-1a8dea1ee57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7b316c-fd27-57d7-ae6d-1a8dea1ee57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451848} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecdec4e8-476e-5e64-bfe1-002886cf49b8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e26320c-f5fc-5d22-962b-bc6fcc8e7c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451849} {:answer/id #uuid "fd978c93-8391-56ee-b944-a6b07dbbf21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd978c93-8391-56ee-b944-a6b07dbbf21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451850} :answer-field/id #uuid "38dc4bf6-46bb-5bfd-8850-b313313b3744" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c81c0d34-9745-5e75-9229-e0ad0c633344" :question/math-academy-id "q-84063" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $\\text{Im}(T)={[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,x=0}$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$\n- **II.** If $\\text{Ker}(T)={[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,y-2z=0,x+z=0}$ then $\\text{rank}(T)=2$\n- **III.** If ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are the columns of $T$ and ${v}_{3}={v}_{1}-{v}_{2}$, then $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{3}$ into ${R}^{3},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=3 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=y{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+z{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}.$ Therefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=2.$ Finally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T) & =3-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Solving $y-2z=0$ for $y,$ we get $y=2z.$ Solving $x+z=0$ for $x,$ we get $x=-z.$ Therefore, any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-z \\\\ 2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=z{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}.$ Therefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=1.$ Finally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T) & =3-\\text{nullity}(T) \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. If the columns of $T$ are such that ${v}_{3}={v}_{1}-{v}_{2},$ then the set of vectors ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent and therefore $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Col}(T)\\ne {R}^{3}.$ Now, according to the matrix invertible theorem, we obtain that $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3139a9d-4709-52dc-b082-fa6e7262b4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451863} {:answer/id #uuid "6611bee2-086e-5458-82d6-29162e06ef7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6611bee2-086e-5458-82d6-29162e06ef7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451864} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b3c705f-a12e-5ec7-9d9e-7cfb964eab33" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80fd8012-3fa3-5669-b4d0-1a4677a6674d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451865} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d74f60-32b7-5c05-af9d-16a41f64d1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4d74f60-32b7-5c05-af9d-16a41f64d1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451866} :answer-field/id #uuid "061f5f16-a1a6-5a40-b334-2790c7680235" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb7b4d4-53de-5934-8e1a-b0b8206b39b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451867} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9d8d40-8af7-502f-800e-af1a162fcfc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f9d8d40-8af7-502f-800e-af1a162fcfc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451868} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5bb764e-2d9e-5196-a9d1-56181fe324ba" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ad99f7f-a225-5eb9-a085-4dc337f7e2b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-86752" :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $D$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $D$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $D$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(D-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +7)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $D$ are $\\lambda =-1$ (with algebraic multiplicity $2$), $\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162013 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c67d532-acd9-5231-a27f-d39084863e01" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Spectral Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c6e59cf-eefe-5e7d-9e31-a8784bb64fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452197} {:answer/id #uuid "21e11fcb-04eb-552c-a533-7cc128693eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21e11fcb-04eb-552c-a533-7cc128693eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452198} :answer-field/id #uuid "99c5561a-1c1f-5380-a23d-ed36c45bd3f7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73d0b8cb-9801-5fc9-a55c-c637e3fd779a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452199} {:answer/id #uuid "f773140f-7c60-560e-8d94-6114e21180eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d0b8cb-9801-5fc9-a55c-c637e3fd779a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452199} :answer-field/id #uuid "b81448bd-7bd9-5f9c-a66a-2e21a29d3fec" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73bd6dbf-2be9-5c2b-8fad-7080e8da1057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452201} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c1e16b-b961-57ac-90e1-29a223838bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c1e16b-b961-57ac-90e1-29a223838bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452202} :answer-field/id #uuid "c352f51f-c826-5af3-a439-3bb54f1ba94c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66a9cbb1-7460-5af7-96d5-cd936a2ef154" :question/math-academy-id "q-95405" :question/problem "Given that $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable\n- **II.** $A$ must have $8$ real and distinct eigenvalues\n- **III.** If $u$ and $v$ are two eigenvectors that correspond to different eigenvalues, then $u⊥v$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real but not necessarily distinct. This occurs when the characteristic polynomial has roots whose (algebraic) multiplicity is greater than $1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues must be orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
